Important Project Constraint 

Minimal / Zero Console ModdingThe Freenet Gaming Node must be designed so that the only change required on the console itself is setting a custom DNS server (pointing it at the PC running the Gaming Node).Key rules:
No custom firmware (CFW) should be required.
No homebrew, patches, or game modifications should be required on the console.
No need to install anything on the console beyond changing DNS settings in the system network configuration.
The Gaming Node + Freenet must handle everything else on the PC side.
The system should work on stock / unmodified consoles whenever the console allows custom DNS (this includes many 3DS, Wii U, Wii, PS3, PS4, Xbox 360, etc. systems).
If a particular console or game later proves that pure DNS redirection is not enough, document it clearly as a limitation, but the default design goal remains: zero console modding, only DNS change + PC-side Gaming Node + Freenet.The finished product should feel like a normal, stable Freenet application that a regular user can install on their computer, start up, point their console’s DNS at it, and play.
